/// React components written in Zyth (module `zyth.react`), compiled to JavaScript by
/// `zyth build --target npm-jsx`: each `@export` function that returns an `Element` becomes a
/// React component, and its parameters its props.
///
///     use zyth.react.{div, h1, button, use_state, Element}
///
///     @export
///     fn Counter(label: str, start: i64 = 0) -> Element {
///         let (count, set_count) = use_state(start)
///         return div(class: "counter") {
///             h1 { "{label}: {count}" }
///             button(on_click: || set_count(count + 1)) { "+1" }
///         }
///     }
///
/// Elements are HTML tags (every element of the HTML standard but the document's own and `var`)
/// and SVG tags (`linear_gradient`, `clip_path`, ... for linearGradient, clipPath) called with
/// props as named arguments (`class`, `on_click`, `aria_label`, `stroke_width` become className,
/// onClick, aria-label, strokeWidth) and a trailing block of children: each value in the block
/// is a child, and `for` and `if` inside it add children. A component with a parameter
/// `children: Element` gets the block it is called with. Hooks: `use_state`,
/// `use_effect(run, deps:)`, `use_layout_effect`, `use_memo(make, deps:)`, `use_callback`,
/// `use_ref(initial)`, `use_reducer(step, first)` (state and a dispatch checked against the
/// reducer's action type), `use_id()`, `use_transition()` (pending, start), `use_deferred_value`.
/// Context: `let theme = create_context("light")` at the top, `provider(theme, value: "dark")
/// { ... }` around children, `use_context(theme)` (typed by the default). react-redux:
/// `use_selector(|s| s.count)` and `use_dispatch()` (the package then names react-redux as a
/// peer dependency).
/// `use_async(make, deps:)` runs `make` after rendering and gives `None` until its value
/// arrives, then the value (it keeps the last value while `deps` changes bring a new one).
///
/// Functions that need tensors, models or anything else JavaScript output does not have run in
/// WebAssembly (the light or full zyth.wasm from the shared runtime package, with WebGPU when
/// there is one). Their calls take time, so a component calls them in `use_async` or in an event handler
/// (`on_click: || set_label(classify(text))`), never while rendering.
/// `use_frame(|t| draw(t))` calls `draw` at every animation frame (`t`: seconds since the
/// component appeared), the next only after the last finished. With `zyth.gfx`, a window made
/// with `gfx.window(..., host: "id")` puts its canvas into the element with that id, so a
/// component renders `div(id: "id")` and draws one frame (`s.frame { f -> ... }`) per call.
/// These run only in JavaScript; `zyth run` refuses them.

/// A React element.
pub struct Element {
    tag: str
}
